  "body": "## What changed\n\nHeidenhain, TinyG and Carvera refuse BORE by name.\nThe counted diagnostic blocks app export with or without a dwell.\n\n## Cause\n\nThese posts expanded a bore into feed-in and rapid-out moves while the spindle kept turning.\nThe chain did not implement the spindle stop required before the retract.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe pins heidenhain_refuses_expanded_bore, tinyg_refuses_expanded_bore and carvera_refuses_expanded_bore failed before the fix and pass after it.\nEach covers zero dwell and a 0.5-second dwell.\nordinary_drilling_remains_available passes for all three posts.\nRestoring each original post separately made its pin fail.\nRestoring each fix made its pin pass.\nThe Heidenhain accepted-cycle test now excludes the refused bore and retains backbore coverage.\nThe quick gate passed 24 post suites and 23 app suites against upstream/main 2f6de7c5.\nThe first gate hit a sandbox denial in the sccache directory.\nThe rerun passed with per-command Cargo settings disabling the cache.\nClippy passed for camcraft-post with all targets and warnings denied.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine ran this change.\nThe GUI, batch gate and release gate were not run.\nThe developer CLI still exposes diagnostic program text.\nThis fix uses the existing app export refusal contract.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1738 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThis applies to all three post scripts.\nPR #1821 adds separate bore tests that expect expanded Heidenhain output and will need reconciliation with this refusal when both land.\nThis branch starts directly from upstream/main 2f6de7c5.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Refuse expanded bores on Heidenhain, TinyG and Carvera because their plain-move chains do not stop the spindle before rapid retract.\n\nFixes #1819\n",
